# Interface definition for thorn Cartoon2DX

IMPLEMENTS: Cartoon2DX

# No INHERITS: of any kind. This thorn owns no grid variables. CarpetX
# calls ApplyCartoonBoundary from apply_boundary_conditions for groups
# whose faces are boundary_t::cartoon (y-ghosts, and x<0 when
# fill_negative_x), according to each group's tensor type and CENTERING.
#
# Tensor type comes from the Einstein Toolkit `tensortypealias` tag
# (Scalar / U or D / DD_sym) -- the same tag old Cartoon2D reads --
# falling back to the CarpetX `parities` tag (1 / 3 / 6 variables)
# used by generated thorns such as CottonmouthZ4c4m. Packed groups
# (AsterX cons_vector) are walked component-wise from parities.
# Untagged 1-variable GFs are treated as scalars. rho is computed
# from PointDesc .x/.y, which are centering-aware.
# Consumers do not need a glue thorn: tag the group and activate
# Cartoon2DX.
#
# Do not add INHERITS: here. An earlier version did
# `INHERITS: CottonmouthZ4c4m`, which forced ADMBaseX/CottonmouthZ4c4m/
# TmunuBaseX to be active whenever Cartoon2DX was, and broke the
# WaveToyX par file ("Implementation 'ADMBASEX' not activated").

USES INCLUDE HEADER: loop.hxx
USES INCLUDE HEADER: loop_device.hxx
USES INCLUDE HEADER: vect.hxx

# Public header providing the driver-independent cartoon math (rho and
# tensor-rotation geometry, 1D Lagrange interpolation). See
# src/cartoon2dx.hxx for details and test/standalone_math_test.cxx for
# its correctness tests. Consuming thorns should add
# "REQUIRES Cartoon2DX" to their own configuration.ccl and
# `#include <cartoon2dx.hxx>`.
INCLUDES HEADER: cartoon2dx.hxx IN cartoon2dx.hxx

# CarpetX-specific ghost-fill glue built on top of the above (GF3D5
# stencil gathering + looping). See src/cartoon2dx_carpetx.hxx.
INCLUDES HEADER: cartoon2dx_carpetx.hxx IN cartoon2dx_carpetx.hxx

# No grid variables of its own.

void FUNCTION ApplyCartoonBoundary( \
  CCTK_POINTER_TO_CONST IN cctkGH, \
  CCTK_INT IN gi, \
  CCTK_INT IN tl)
PROVIDES FUNCTION ApplyCartoonBoundary WITH Cartoon2DX_ApplyBoundary LANGUAGE C
